# Review / commit cycle (default)

Michael reviews before every commit. This overrides any “commit as you go” or cloud-agent auto-commit habit.

## Do

- Implement a **self-contained, coherently related** chunk of a phase.
- Leave work **uncommitted** and ask Michael to review.
- Commit **only after** explicit confirmation (e.g. “looks good, commit” / “please commit”).
- Aim for a commit history of **relatable chunks** — not one giant dump, not tiny noise commits.

## Do not

- Commit, amend, push, or open/update a PR until Michael asks for that action in the same message (or a later one).
- Treat “please proceed” on *implementation* as permission to commit.
- Split so finely that review becomes tedious, or batch unrelated work into one review.

## Chunk size

Prefer one review/commit per logical unit (e.g. “move helper into impl/”, “split islab.hpp”, “update includes + tests”). A full multi-week feature may span many cycles; a single-file typo fix may be one.
